Package: pc3host
Version: @VERSION@
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Peter Mather <uktailwind@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/UKTailwind/FUZIX
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, libx11-6, libxrandr2
Description: Pico Computer 3 BASIC environment for a PC
 The Pico Computer 3's MMBasic toolchain, hosted on Linux: mmbc
 translates MMBasic to C, cc compiles it to bytecode, bcrun runs it,
 and pc3d shows the PC3's screen in a window and takes its keyboard.
 The programs are the PC3's own, built for a PC.  The tools are
 statically linked; pc3d uses the system's X11 libraries.
 .
 Run `pc3` for a shell with the tools on the PATH, or `pc3 cc -r
 prog.bas` to build and run a program.  Examples are in
 /opt/pc3/share/examples, documentation in /opt/pc3/share/doc/pc3host,
 and the MMBasic translator's own directory - sources, runtime, tests
 and samples - in /opt/pc3/share/mmb2c.
